# JVM options baked into every installer, all operating systems.
#
# ${user.home} is resolved by Spring at RUN TIME on the target machine, not by
# Maven at build time: this file is read directly by jpackage and never
# filtered, and jpackage leaves ${...} untouched (verified). Putting the
# writable state under the user's home lets the app run even when installed in
# a read-only location (Program Files, /Applications, /opt).
#
# Paths may be redirected from outside the jar: LicensePropertyGuard pins only
# the license *switches*, never paths.
--java-options
-Dfile.encoding=UTF-8
--java-options
-Dspring.datasource.url=jdbc:h2:file:${user.home}/.libertyshop/data/libertyshop
--java-options
-Dliberoshop.license.path=${user.home}/.libertyshop/license/libero-shop.lic
--java-options
-Dliberoshop.mobile.downloads-dir=${user.home}/.libertyshop/downloads
# The installed application has no window: show its state and its menu (open,
# stop, restart, update, quit) in the notification area. See desktop.ServerTray.
--java-options
-Dliberoshop.tray.enabled=true
